1
00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:10,800
"Blue Lips"

2
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:13,800
(Episode 13)

3
00:02:02,139 --> 00:02:03,139
You're back.

4
00:02:06,219 --> 00:02:07,480
What exactly happened?

5
00:02:07,619 --> 00:02:08,380
Was it him?
No, sis.

6
00:02:13,219 --> 00:02:14,980
Mr. Teng, I told you, didn't I?

7
00:02:15,179 --> 00:02:16,738
Don't use the little
favors you've done for him

8
00:02:16,739 --> 00:02:17,619
to manipulate him.

9
00:02:17,739 --> 00:02:19,000
Sis, it really wasn't him.

10
00:02:21,599 --> 00:02:22,658
What is it then?

11
00:02:22,659 --> 00:02:23,519
Just spit it out!

12
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:24,595
You're killing me with the suspense!

13
00:02:24,619 --> 00:02:25,619
Sis, I...

14
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:26,340
Sis.

15
00:02:26,820 --> 00:02:27,820
Let me explain.

16
00:02:28,420 --> 00:02:29,960
We actually ran into a little trouble.

17
00:02:30,260 --> 00:02:31,260
It's no big deal.

18
00:02:31,699 --> 00:02:32,699
It's just that...

19
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:34,599
Shixian was previously

20
00:02:34,820 --> 00:02:36,400
scammed by an old lady, remember?

21
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:38,320
Her son came looking for him today.

22
00:02:38,659 --> 00:02:39,756
He happened to run into Shixian,

23
00:02:39,780 --> 00:02:41,039
and they got into a fight.

24
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:43,059
But I stepped in and stopped it.

25
00:02:44,260 --> 00:02:46,060
I also took him to the
ER to get checked out.

26
00:02:46,260 --> 00:02:47,700
Just a few scrapes, nothing serious.

27
00:02:48,619 --> 00:02:49,619
Let me see.

28
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:56,400
Does it hurt?

29
00:02:57,380 --> 00:02:58,380
No.

30
00:02:59,679 --> 00:03:00,679
Did you call the cops?

31
00:03:02,219 --> 00:03:03,219
No.

32
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:05,540
Then what you just said...

33
00:03:07,460 --> 00:03:08,460
I lied to them.

34
00:03:09,159 --> 00:03:11,359
The cops can't do much
about this kind of thing anyway.

35
00:03:11,619 --> 00:03:12,059
Then...

36
00:03:12,060 --> 00:03:13,900
Are you really going to
give him that 150,000?

37
00:03:14,900 --> 00:03:15,900
What 150,000?

38
00:03:17,420 --> 00:03:18,420
It was just...

39
00:03:18,559 --> 00:03:19,659
my stalling tactic.

40
00:03:20,179 --> 00:03:20,699
I told them

41
00:03:20,900 --> 00:03:22,198
I'd pay them 150,000 next week.

42
00:03:22,199 --> 00:03:23,199
They agreed.

43
00:03:23,320 --> 00:03:24,699
Money doesn't grow on trees.

44
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:26,400
I can't just hand it over like that.

45
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:27,920
Then are you...

46
00:03:28,260 --> 00:03:29,260
going empty-handed?

47
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:31,240
To deal with scumbags like them,

48
00:03:31,539 --> 00:03:33,119
you have to fight fire with fire.

49
00:03:33,280 --> 00:03:34,280
I have plenty of ways.

50
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:35,320
Trust me.

51
00:03:37,119 --> 00:03:38,659
I've always found it weird.

52
00:03:39,199 --> 00:03:41,360
The old lady gets hit one second,

53
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:42,980
and her son shows up the next.

54
00:03:43,739 --> 00:03:45,259
They don't even have a medical report.

55
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:46,599
Logically speaking,

56
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:48,399
even if people like
them didn't have a report,

57
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:49,679
they'd forge one.

58
00:03:50,179 --> 00:03:51,460
These people are full of holes.

59
00:03:51,519 --> 00:03:53,079
They're easy to handle. Leave it to me.

60
00:03:53,239 --> 00:03:54,896
Then I'll go with you when the time comes.

61
00:03:54,920 --> 00:03:55,920
You definitely can't go.

62
00:03:56,159 --> 00:03:56,860
You're too hot-headed.

63
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,280
What if you start fighting them?

64
00:03:59,920 --> 00:04:00,960
Let your sister rest easy.

65
00:04:11,219 --> 00:04:12,219
Is she asleep?

66
00:04:16,139 --> 00:04:16,780
Why did you

67
00:04:16,781 --> 00:04:18,500
just blurt everything out today?

68
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:20,960
Everyone in the hospital knows about it.

69
00:04:21,099 --> 00:04:22,019
Even if I didn't say anything,

70
00:04:22,020 --> 00:04:23,259
with the nurses and
caretakers coming and going,

71
00:04:23,260 --> 00:04:24,260
in and out all day,

72
00:04:24,519 --> 00:04:25,916
word would get out sooner or later.

73
00:04:25,940 --> 00:04:27,219
She'd be even angrier then.

74
00:04:29,159 --> 00:04:30,159
Besides,

75
00:04:30,539 --> 00:04:31,820
we're family.

76
00:04:32,280 --> 00:04:34,159
Family needs to talk things over.

77
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:36,160
Otherwise, how can
we call ourselves family?

78
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:41,320
Oh, right.

79
00:04:41,380 --> 00:04:42,380
Here.

80
00:04:42,980 --> 00:04:43,980
Take this.

81
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:46,800
What is it?

82
00:04:47,019 --> 00:04:48,839
Last time your sister couldn't reach you,

83
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:49,840
she was worried sick.

84
00:04:50,039 --> 00:04:52,219
You need to let her know
where you are at all times.

85
00:04:53,539 --> 00:04:54,659
The apps are all downloaded.

86
00:04:54,980 --> 00:04:56,300
The system is the same as before.

87
00:04:56,619 --> 00:04:57,619
It's easy to use.

88
00:04:58,760 --> 00:04:59,760
Thank you.

89
00:05:00,199 --> 00:05:01,199
No need to thank me.

90
00:05:02,320 --> 00:05:03,559
I will definitely...

91
00:05:03,679 --> 00:05:04,679
Definitely what?

92
00:05:04,739 --> 00:05:05,739
Pay me back?

93
00:05:06,380 --> 00:05:07,420
You can never pay me back.

94
00:05:11,239 --> 00:05:12,239
By the way,

95
00:05:12,280 --> 00:05:13,139
before I came over,

96
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:14,280
I made dinner at home.

97
00:05:14,460 --> 00:05:15,920
Go back and take a hot shower.

98
00:05:16,119 --> 00:05:17,296
Just heat up the food and eat.

99
00:05:17,320 --> 00:05:18,320
Then go to bed early.

100
00:05:19,940 --> 00:05:20,940
Be good.

101
00:05:37,659 --> 00:05:38,780
You actually...

102
00:05:39,699 --> 00:05:40,880
knew all along, didn't you?

103
00:05:44,519 --> 00:05:46,760
I'm not with you for the money.

104
00:05:50,360 --> 00:05:51,360
I know.

105
00:05:53,599 --> 00:05:55,159
Then why did you pretend not to know?

106
00:05:55,659 --> 00:05:56,840
And keep sending me money?

107
00:05:59,260 --> 00:06:00,260
Shixian,

108
00:06:01,420 --> 00:06:09,280
If the bond between people is built with
money, it easily crumbles, it isn't pure.

109
00:06:10,139 --> 00:06:11,199
Once this bond

110
00:06:11,519 --> 00:06:12,960
is stripped of money and interests,

111
00:06:13,559 --> 00:06:14,820
it becomes very strong.

112
00:06:16,619 --> 00:06:17,840
I want our bond to be strong.

113
00:06:18,579 --> 00:06:19,579
But before,

114
00:06:20,199 --> 00:06:22,199
I always thought you'd regret it.

115
00:06:22,780 --> 00:06:24,180
You'd feel we weren't a good match.

116
00:06:24,440 --> 00:06:26,260
That's why I tied us together with money.

117
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:28,980
So you could walk away more easily.

118
00:06:32,280 --> 00:06:33,280
Teng Mo,

119
00:06:35,559 --> 00:06:37,139
feelings can't be calculated.

120
00:06:38,239 --> 00:06:39,839
And they certainly can't be manipulated.

121
00:06:41,320 --> 00:06:43,440
They won't follow your original plan.

122
00:06:45,619 --> 00:06:46,619
I understand.

123
00:06:47,219 --> 00:06:48,320
That's why I came back.

124
00:06:50,119 --> 00:06:51,119
I'm glad

125
00:06:53,079 --> 00:06:54,079
we still have time.

126
00:07:00,579 --> 00:07:00,880
Let's go.

127
00:07:01,219 --> 00:07:02,219
Shixian.

128
00:07:02,659 --> 00:07:03,659
Let's go home.

129
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:39,900
Did you eat?

130
00:07:41,960 --> 00:07:42,960
I ate.

131
00:07:44,980 --> 00:07:46,400
How's the phone?

132
00:07:50,760 --> 00:07:51,760
It's great.

133
00:07:52,099 --> 00:07:53,139
Did you eat?

134
00:07:54,960 --> 00:07:55,960
I did.

135
00:07:57,199 --> 00:07:59,639
The food near the hospital is awful.

136
00:08:07,219 --> 00:08:09,019
Is my sister doing okay?

137
00:08:15,079 --> 00:08:16,079
She's doing fine.

138
00:08:16,300 --> 00:08:17,580
She's lying down reading a book.

139
00:08:19,039 --> 00:08:20,039
What should I do?

140
00:08:20,479 --> 00:08:21,939
I'm already starting to miss you.

141
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:26,500
Then I'll head over early tomorrow.

142
00:08:26,939 --> 00:08:27,239
Don't.

143
00:08:27,659 --> 00:08:28,420
Get some good sleep.

144
00:08:28,600 --> 00:08:29,600
Sleep in.

145
00:08:35,939 --> 00:08:37,220
I miss you so much.

146
00:08:42,969 --> 00:08:45,476
[TN: Auto-suggest says: What are we gonna
do? | I really miss you | I love you so much]

147
00:08:46,220 --> 00:08:47,779
The bad things are all in the past.

148
00:08:48,319 --> 00:08:49,319
From now on,

149
00:08:49,619 --> 00:08:50,779
come rain or shine,

150
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:52,635
through freezing winters
or scorching summers,

151
00:08:52,659 --> 00:08:54,020
I will be by your side.

152
00:08:55,500 --> 00:08:57,800
Every memorable day in your life,

153
00:08:58,300 --> 00:08:59,300
I will be there.

154
00:09:00,300 --> 00:09:01,699
As long as you don't push me away,

155
00:09:02,340 --> 00:09:03,600
I will always be here.

156
00:10:28,260 --> 00:10:29,260
Hello?

157
00:10:30,699 --> 00:10:31,699
I know about it.

158
00:10:32,539 --> 00:10:33,800
I'll arrange the guys for you.

159
00:10:43,760 --> 00:10:44,999
Can you handle it alone?

160
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:46,720
How about letting Shixian go with you?

161
00:10:46,819 --> 00:10:47,399
It's fine.

162
00:10:47,760 --> 00:10:48,760
I can handle it.

163
00:10:49,119 --> 00:10:50,000
Shixian has a hot temper.

164
00:10:50,060 --> 00:10:51,356
If he goes, things could
easily get out of hand.

165
00:10:51,380 --> 00:10:52,380
Don't worry.

166
00:10:53,220 --> 00:10:54,220
I'll get going then.

167
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:28,100
This is between you and Xiao Wu,
[but] I'm still a little worried.

168
00:11:29,380 --> 00:11:30,580
Alright, you're a true friend.

169
00:11:30,819 --> 00:11:31,239
Let's go.

170
00:11:31,640 --> 00:11:32,640
Let's go.

171
00:11:39,100 --> 00:11:40,500
Can you just sit down for a second?

172
00:11:41,340 --> 00:11:42,379
Pacing back and forth...

173
00:11:42,380 --> 00:11:43,939
You're making me dizzy.

174
00:11:44,659 --> 00:11:46,020
Got ants in your pants?

175
00:11:47,340 --> 00:11:48,020
I...

176
00:11:48,279 --> 00:11:49,619
just got up to stretch my legs.

177
00:11:52,460 --> 00:11:53,776
There's no need to worry so much.

178
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:55,500
Teng Mo knows what he's doing.

179
00:11:56,699 --> 00:11:57,699
I...

180
00:11:57,859 --> 00:11:58,859
Am I worried?

181
00:11:59,199 --> 00:11:59,520
Well...

182
00:11:59,779 --> 00:12:00,779
Not really.

183
00:12:01,119 --> 00:12:01,640
I'm not.

184
00:12:01,739 --> 00:12:02,979
There's nothing to worry about.

185
00:12:04,100 --> 00:12:05,100
You're not worried?

186
00:12:05,460 --> 00:12:07,219
Then why are you pacing around in circles?

187
00:12:07,220 --> 00:12:08,399
Back and forth.

188
00:12:09,300 --> 00:12:11,780
Or is it that you can't bear to
be away from him for a second?

189
00:12:12,819 --> 00:12:13,819
Sis!

190
00:12:13,899 --> 00:12:14,979
What are you talking about?

191
00:12:27,199 --> 00:12:28,380
Bro, this is a hospital.

192
00:12:28,479 --> 00:12:29,479
You can't smoke here.

193
00:12:34,699 --> 00:12:35,699
Hello?

194
00:12:35,779 --> 00:12:36,859
How are things on your end?

195
00:12:37,039 --> 00:12:37,800
Come downstairs for a sec.

196
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:39,040
Don't let your sister know.

197
00:12:40,020 --> 00:12:41,439
Okay, I'm heading down now.

198
00:12:43,359 --> 00:12:44,639
Sis, I'm stepping out for a bit.

199
00:12:47,760 --> 00:12:48,760
This kid.

200
00:12:56,300 --> 00:12:57,539
Why bring them here?

201
00:13:02,880 --> 00:13:03,880
Brother Wu,

202
00:13:04,060 --> 00:13:05,660
about us trying to extort you last time,

203
00:13:05,739 --> 00:13:06,819
we were in the wrong.

204
00:13:07,220 --> 00:13:08,940
Please be the bigger person and forgive us.

205
00:13:09,060 --> 00:13:10,460
Just let us off the hook this once.

206
00:13:14,079 --> 00:13:15,159
They're apologizing to you.

207
00:13:15,659 --> 00:13:16,380
You can accept it,

208
00:13:16,381 --> 00:13:17,600
or you can choose not to.

209
00:13:20,920 --> 00:13:21,920
It's up to you.

210
00:13:25,819 --> 00:13:27,739
I've got elderly parents
and young kids to feed.

211
00:13:27,779 --> 00:13:30,199
My whole family depends on me to survive.

212
00:13:30,520 --> 00:13:31,739
I can't go to jail!

213
00:13:32,260 --> 00:13:34,000
My old mother is already seventy.

214
00:13:34,220 --> 00:13:35,239
You can't bear to see her

215
00:13:35,659 --> 00:13:37,140
bury her own son, right?

216
00:13:37,880 --> 00:13:38,880
Yeah, Brother Wu.

217
00:13:38,920 --> 00:13:39,920
I was wrong.

218
00:13:39,960 --> 00:13:40,460
At the time,

219
00:13:40,619 --> 00:13:41,859
I just had a moment of madness.

220
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:43,140
Seeing a young guy like you

221
00:13:43,560 --> 00:13:45,060
taking care of a sick sister,

222
00:13:45,180 --> 00:13:45,979
I thought you'd be an easy target.
So I came up with

223
00:13:47,100 --> 00:13:48,380
the terrible idea to extort you.

224
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:50,000
I was wrong.

225
00:13:50,659 --> 00:13:51,939
Please be the bigger person.

226
00:13:52,260 --> 00:13:53,399
Show some mercy.

227
00:13:53,779 --> 00:13:55,060
Don't stoop to my level.

228
00:13:55,380 --> 00:13:56,739
If you're still mad, hit me.

229
00:13:57,539 --> 00:13:58,199
Hit me right here.
Slap me a few times.

230
00:13:59,460 --> 00:14:00,460
I absolutely won't dodge.

231
00:14:00,859 --> 00:14:01,859
Brother Wu,

232
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:07,000
do you still want the 150,000?

233
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:09,000
No, we don't.

234
00:14:09,100 --> 00:14:09,939
We don't want a single cent.

235
00:14:10,119 --> 00:14:11,119
If you're still angry,

236
00:14:11,359 --> 00:14:12,140
just beat us up.

237
00:14:12,220 --> 00:14:13,220
Yeah.

238
00:14:13,899 --> 00:14:14,939
That's so despicable.

239
00:14:15,119 --> 00:14:16,439
Picking on honest people.

240
00:14:17,060 --> 00:14:17,659
Exactly.

241
00:14:17,960 --> 00:14:19,255
People are already having a hard time,

242
00:14:19,279 --> 00:14:20,515
and you still try to extort them.

243
00:14:20,539 --> 00:14:21,260
So shameless.

244
00:14:21,520 --> 00:14:22,520
Exactly.

245
00:14:22,619 --> 00:14:24,499
And you have the nerve
to bring up your mother.

246
00:14:24,720 --> 00:14:26,515
Do you think the rest of us
just popped out of thin air?

247
00:14:26,539 --> 00:14:27,859
And deserve to be bullied by you?

248
00:14:28,020 --> 00:14:29,020
So evil.

249
00:14:29,439 --> 00:14:30,599
What kind of people are they?

250
00:14:32,840 --> 00:14:33,938
You should tell him off.

251
00:14:33,939 --> 00:14:34,939
This kind of thing...

252
00:14:39,100 --> 00:14:40,100
From now on,

253
00:14:40,460 --> 00:14:42,039
don't let me ever see you again.

254
00:14:43,100 --> 00:14:44,500
Brother Wu, don't worry.

255
00:14:44,939 --> 00:14:45,979
From now on in Jinyang,

256
00:14:46,380 --> 00:14:47,659
you definitely won't see us.

257
00:14:47,899 --> 00:14:48,938
If we see you,

258
00:14:48,939 --> 00:14:49,899
we'll take a detour.
Yeah.

259
00:14:50,880 --> 00:14:52,320
You'd better remember what you said.

260
00:14:52,819 --> 00:14:53,819
I remember.

261
00:14:53,939 --> 00:14:55,619
I won't forget it for the rest of my life.

262
00:15:00,260 --> 00:15:01,260
Get lost.

263
00:15:03,239 --> 00:15:04,239
Let's go, let's go.

264
00:15:14,659 --> 00:15:15,659
Let's go see your sister.

265
00:15:25,979 --> 00:15:27,060
What beautiful flowers.

266
00:15:27,659 --> 00:15:28,659
Thank you all.

267
00:15:29,039 --> 00:15:30,039
You're welcome.

268
00:15:30,119 --> 00:15:31,779
We just heard about Xiao Wu's situation.

269
00:15:31,979 --> 00:15:33,499
We should have come to see you sooner.

270
00:15:33,699 --> 00:15:35,140
Wishing you a speedy recovery.

271
00:15:35,640 --> 00:15:36,640
Thank you.

272
00:15:37,340 --> 00:15:39,140
I don't think I caught your name, sir.

273
00:15:39,859 --> 00:15:40,859
My last name is Guan.

274
00:15:41,020 --> 00:15:42,020
Guan Zhenghao.

275
00:15:43,600 --> 00:15:43,979
Sis,

276
00:15:44,439 --> 00:15:46,340
Guan Zhenghao is a
friend I met at Blue Moon.

277
00:15:46,779 --> 00:15:47,460
He's really amazing.

278
00:15:47,560 --> 00:15:48,560
He even owns a company.

279
00:15:48,720 --> 00:15:50,000
That crowd outside just now,

280
00:15:50,279 --> 00:15:50,600
they're all...

281
00:15:50,739 --> 00:15:51,739
They're all my employees.

282
00:15:55,380 --> 00:15:56,539
I started a company.

283
00:15:56,899 --> 00:15:59,180
Xiao Wu and Teng Mo are
both good friends of mine.

284
00:16:00,739 --> 00:16:02,158
I was worried before

285
00:16:02,159 --> 00:16:04,919
that it wasn't appropriate for
Shixian to work in a place like a bar.

286
00:16:04,979 --> 00:16:06,478
But seeing how all of you

287
00:16:06,479 --> 00:16:07,559
take such good care of him,

288
00:16:08,159 --> 00:16:09,399
it seems I was overthinking it.

289
00:16:10,760 --> 00:16:11,760
Don't worry.

290
00:16:11,939 --> 00:16:12,939
Xiao Wu gets along great

291
00:16:13,319 --> 00:16:14,539
with everyone at the bar.

292
00:16:14,659 --> 00:16:16,099
Plus, the work there is pretty easy.

293
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:16,619
Just...

294
00:16:16,960 --> 00:16:18,039
singing and stuff, right?

295
00:16:21,239 --> 00:16:22,420
That's really wonderful.

296
00:16:22,979 --> 00:16:24,236
Actually, regarding
what happened this time,

297
00:16:24,260 --> 00:16:25,540
we really owe it to Brother Hao.

298
00:16:25,979 --> 00:16:26,979
It was nothing.

299
00:16:30,960 --> 00:16:31,340
By the way,

300
00:16:31,960 --> 00:16:33,079
why did they suddenly

301
00:16:33,500 --> 00:16:34,500
become so obedient?

302
00:16:35,180 --> 00:16:36,538
Actually, that old lady

303
00:16:36,539 --> 00:16:37,539
wasn't hurt at all.

304
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,100
I recorded a video of it.

305
00:16:39,318 --> 00:16:41,398
Then Brother Hao showed him the video.

306
00:16:41,819 --> 00:16:43,619
I even heard he
threatened to break his legs.

307
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:47,359
No, I didn't.
Just scaring them a bit.

308
00:16:48,220 --> 00:16:49,220
Right.

309
00:16:50,479 --> 00:16:51,818
Then they started crying their eyes out,

310
00:16:51,819 --> 00:16:52,420
kneeling down,
and apologizing.

311
00:16:53,420 --> 00:16:54,119
With acting skills like that,

312
00:16:54,359 --> 00:16:55,999
running scams is a waste of their talent.

313
00:16:56,399 --> 00:16:57,536
Don't listen to his nonsense.

314
00:16:57,560 --> 00:16:58,875
I really just scared them a little.

315
00:16:58,899 --> 00:16:59,760
I wasn't planning on getting physical.

316
00:16:59,761 --> 00:17:01,001
It's a society governed by law.

317
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:04,520
And then?

318
00:17:06,180 --> 00:17:07,180
Then,

319
00:17:07,619 --> 00:17:08,220
I just

320
00:17:08,300 --> 00:17:10,659
gave them a quick lesson
on civil and criminal law.

321
00:17:10,979 --> 00:17:12,619
If this counts as extortion,

322
00:17:12,859 --> 00:17:14,299
they could get seven or eight years.

323
00:17:14,340 --> 00:17:15,180
That scared them even more.

324
00:17:15,319 --> 00:17:16,679
So they hurried over to apologize.

325
00:17:19,659 --> 00:17:21,139
You really know how to handle things.

326
00:17:21,779 --> 00:17:23,420
They were just too arrogant.

327
00:17:23,520 --> 00:17:26,320
It was only a matter of time before
they messed with the wrong person.

328
00:17:29,020 --> 00:17:30,800
We really owe you all for this.

329
00:17:31,020 --> 00:17:32,479
Otherwise, for us,

330
00:17:32,619 --> 00:17:34,219
it would have made things so much worse.

331
00:17:35,100 --> 00:17:36,100
Not at all.

332
00:17:37,239 --> 00:17:37,760
We'll leave you to it.

333
00:17:38,039 --> 00:17:39,279
We won't bother you any longer.

334
00:17:39,579 --> 00:17:40,079
Shixian,

335
00:17:40,260 --> 00:17:41,340
go see them out.

336
00:17:52,260 --> 00:17:53,260
Wu Shixian.

337
00:17:53,939 --> 00:17:54,939
Take this.

338
00:17:57,260 --> 00:17:57,899
No, no.

339
00:17:58,180 --> 00:17:59,755
It's already more than
enough that you came to visit.

340
00:17:59,779 --> 00:18:00,779
I can't accept this.

341
00:18:00,960 --> 00:18:01,960
Just take it.

342
00:18:02,039 --> 00:18:03,679
It's a little something from Brother Hao.

343
00:18:03,800 --> 00:18:04,800
For your sister.

344
00:18:13,159 --> 00:18:14,159
Thank you.

345
00:18:15,220 --> 00:18:16,220
I didn't expect

346
00:18:16,539 --> 00:18:18,739
you guys to come all the
way upstairs to see my sister.

347
00:18:19,020 --> 00:18:20,060
She was really happy, too.

348
00:18:20,880 --> 00:18:21,380
No need to see us out.

349
00:18:21,560 --> 00:18:23,715
I'm going to accompany Curly
to get his stitches removed later.

350
00:18:23,739 --> 00:18:24,739
What happened?

351
00:18:25,140 --> 00:18:26,340
How did Curly get hurt?

352
00:18:27,359 --> 00:18:29,356
A couple of days ago, an
enemy came looking for revenge.

353
00:18:29,380 --> 00:18:30,659
Curly took a knife for me.

354
00:18:32,579 --> 00:18:33,579
Is it resolved?

355
00:18:34,239 --> 00:18:35,239
It's resolved.

356
00:18:37,079 --> 00:18:38,079
Be careful.

357
00:18:38,220 --> 00:18:39,700
How many lives do you think you have?

358
00:18:41,380 --> 00:18:42,380
I plan to

359
00:18:42,739 --> 00:18:44,439
finish one last thing and then

360
00:18:44,840 --> 00:18:45,840
wash my hands of it.

361
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:47,939
I'll take Curly and live a peaceful life.

362
00:18:48,699 --> 00:18:49,699
Enough about me.

363
00:18:50,319 --> 00:18:51,560
His sister's condition

364
00:18:53,600 --> 00:18:54,600
isn't very optimistic.

365
00:18:54,840 --> 00:18:55,920
A heart and lung transplant

366
00:18:56,239 --> 00:18:57,279
costs 1.5 million.

367
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:02,079
And there's no suitable match yet.

368
00:19:02,779 --> 00:19:04,560
Besides, with her current condition,

369
00:19:05,920 --> 00:19:07,240
she's not really fit for surgery.

370
00:19:09,500 --> 00:19:10,760
So that means she...

371
00:19:12,880 --> 00:19:14,319
His sister is still so young.

372
00:19:17,779 --> 00:19:18,819
Let's not talk about this.

373
00:19:19,100 --> 00:19:20,199
We'll do the best we can.

374
00:19:20,680 --> 00:19:21,680
As for the rest,

375
00:19:21,899 --> 00:19:22,899
it's up to God.

376
00:19:25,399 --> 00:19:26,399
Of course.

377
00:19:26,520 --> 00:19:28,080
If there's anything you need help with,

378
00:19:28,220 --> 00:19:29,340
just tell me directly.

379
00:19:31,859 --> 00:19:32,859
Thanks, Brother Hao.

380
00:19:36,720 --> 00:19:37,020
Let's go.

381
00:19:37,279 --> 00:19:38,279
I'll walk you out.
